  (text "SOUND CHIP: the YM2612 and the 3.3V to 5V buffers\nTwo 74HCT541 buffers at 5V turn the Pico's 3.3V signals into solid 5V. 100 ohm resistors on every chip pin protect the YM2612.\nThe bus is write-only: /RD is tied high and /CS low, so the chip listens whenever /WR pulses. /IRQ is not used.\nClock: the Pico makes 7.667 MHz on GP21 and the buffer lifts it to 5V (its 33 ohm resistor is fitted). For exact Genesis pitch,\nfit a 7.670454 MHz 5V oscillator can in X1 and its 33 ohm resistor, and leave out the buffer's 33 ohm.\nWindow lights: D1 and D2 sit beside the socket, angled across the chip, so its markings catch the light." (at 25.4 22.86 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 17d8bc51-d2ca-55ea-a954-b6bff2fb6010)
  )
  (text "Decoupling: one 100nF at each 74HCT541, two at the YM2612 (VCC pin 23, A.VCC pin 22),\none for X1, plus 10uF bulk at the YM2612." (at 261.62 193.04 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid a844e995-be5d-5113-95dc-a934a737590d)
  )
)
